KG42.register("source_edge_archive-cdd27aa8487e99bb1affad74",{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-bebd346528bbcf18","target":"KG31-e2bea6d6e2936fab","source_occurrence_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"405acaaf10cbb318a76441e499026ecb0c8be1098e885e7aac31a87cb601c68d","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction. The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","target_definition":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. State-of-the-Art","anchor_text":"ge revenues for stakeholders [28], [29]. However, one similar- or- ity among most of the above menti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"the proposed modiﬁed auction scheme studied in Section IV 0) can be adopted in each time slot t = 1,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"paper_scope_note":"Initial selection boundary, removal of marginal participants, Stackelberg price, and spatial response are kept separate; this is limited to component use in this auction protocol and does not prove a unique equilibrium or real-world operation."}});
